Subject: [PATCH 2/2] P8 round 2: no duplicate POSTs; ambiguity and persistence
 failure explicit

broker_io.py (proposal, not wired into any bot):
- Ownership: only the caller whose INSERT creates the intent may POST; losers get
  the existing state with 0 POSTs (no raw IntegrityError).
- Compare-and-set transitions; terminal ACCEPTED/REJECTED never overwritten.
  REJECTED only from SUBMITTING with submit_attempts == 1.
- Absence is never inferred: NOT_FOUND_AFTER_WINDOW retired; list is positive
  evidence only; resubmit() disabled (read-only reconcile, never POSTs).
- SubmitResult.order_id on every path; persisted/persistence_error fields;
  NOT_SUBMITTED and CONFLICT states. No exception escapes after a POST,
  including store read failures (found in self-review).
- sqlite connections now closed (contextlib.closing).

Tests: round-2 suite 15 (14 fail on eddcdda, 15 pass); existing 30 pass with 3
expectations changed (documented in ROUND2_REVIEW.md, safety assertions kept).
Timeout/deadline corrections and paper-plan revision remain OPEN.
